    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the mean value of the measures of the three interior angles of any triangle, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the properties of a triangle's interior angles:**\n   The sum of the interior angles of any triangle is always \\(180^\\circ\\).\n\n2. **Define the mean value:**\n   The mean value of the measures of the three interior angles is calculated by dividing the sum of the angles by the number of angles. In this case, the number of angles is 3.\n\n3. **Calculate the mean:**\n   The mean value \\(M\\) is given by the formula:\n   \\[\n   M = \\frac{\\text{Sum of the angles}}{\\text{Number of angles}}\n   \\]\n   Substituting the known values:\n   \\[\n   M = \\frac{180^\\circ}{3}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Perform the division:**\n   \\[\n   M = 60^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the mean value of the measures of the three interior angles of any triangle is \\(\\boxed{60}\\).",
